  "equipment_type": "Process PID controller",
  "applies_to": "Valve Pro VC-88 digital PID process controllers on Modbus, read by a BASgatewayLX.",
  "summary": "Gateway profile for the VC-88 controller: 215 objects (30 AI, 159 AO, 26 BI), all polled. Outputs carry the command register, loop control signals and the full configuration (input types, scaling, alarms, PID sets, set points SP1-SP4, programmer segments); inputs give version, status bits (auto/manual, tuning, alarms, errors), measured values and the current set point.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet IP"
  ],
  "firmware": null,
  "default_device_instance": null,
  "access_inferred": true,
  "notes": [
    "Built from Contemporary Controls' BASgatewayLX Modbus device profile VC_88_Controller_a_LX.csv; the profile maps the registers in the VC-88 Modbus register list (https://www.ccontrols.com/support/dp/VC-88_09D.pdf).",
    "Object instances are the ones this profile assigns when it is loaded into the gateway. A site that edited or rebuilt the profile may use different instances.",
    "All 215 rows are flagged for polling in the profile, so every object is served to BACnet once the profile is loaded.",
    "The CSV has no read/write column: Analog/Binary Inputs are read-only and Analog/Binary Outputs are commandable (priority array), which is how the gateway maps them (access inferred). Descriptions give the Modbus register each object reads.",
    "Some names appear more than once in the profile as published (Measured value PV; Current set point value SP; Indication for the lower threshold of the analog main input...); they are kept as printed and told apart by instance.",
    "Measured value PV appears twice: BI 29 reads only bit 15 of register 404007, while AI 201 (register 407001) carries the value itself."
  ],
  "source": {
    "title": "BASgatewayLX Modbus device profile VC_88_Controller_a",
    "doc_number": "VC_88_Controller_a_LX.csv",
    "revision_date": null,
    "url": "https://www.ccontrols.com/support/dp/ValveProVC-88.zip"
  },
  "integration": {
